# Banter in The Crimson Monastery (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is crimson_monastery): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ mon_ground_01_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:mon_ground and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Spiked black walls, red glass, and the air smells like a sour butcher's tab. The house is marking the deck.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Those statues are weeping real blood, Silas, with no pump I can see. Rather thin, though.
interject name:silas_vane: And the hall doors have the spikes pointing inward. Management really trusts the regulars.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Leave me a drop off the pulpit, darling. I've never studied masonry that bleeds on command.
interject name:silas_vane: Take a whole vial. Just don't ask me to bet on anything in that Dead Larder.
endif
-> END

~ mon_upper_02_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:mon_ground and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: This balustrade's set square, Tobin. Though the red glass is murder on ledger work.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Never mind the glass. Smell those candles. That's no beeswax. That's rendered fat.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Leaves a greasy soot on everything. And two chambers locked against inspection.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep two paces between me and those wicks. I'd sooner chew old ink than catch a fat-spark.
interject name:rook_coldwake: I'll walk on the candle side and keep the shield between the flame and your straw.
endif
-> END

~ mon_stables_03_lucan_delphine
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:delphine_ravelle and at:mon_stables and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Delphine. Boxes in the dead trees. Bat hounds, if my nose hasn't forgotten its schooling.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Charming lodgings. Look at those little eyes opening in the bark like the cheap seats.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Terribly cramped kennels, and right over a prisoners' wagon. A full point off. Barnaby agrees.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness just made a pun about barking up the wrong tree. I may drown him in the trough.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Please restrain yourself. The warhorses are nervous enough already.
endif
-> END

~ mon_bell_tower_04_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:mon_bell_tower and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Fouled straw and gnawed bones on the landing. This staircase is a tragedy for velvet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The bacteria in those dog beds, Delphine. I could harvest three diseases before the ladder.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Keep your vials corked till we're through that trapdoor. The stink is flattening my voice.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The draught from that window keeps it cool. The marrow in those bones has barely soured.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: You've a crooked idea of a silver lining, Cordelia. Hold the rungs steady.
endif
-> END

~ mon_sanctum_05_rook_silas
if name:rook_coldwake and name:silas_vane and at:mon_sanctum and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: An altar on an island, ringed by open blood with no grating. That's a slip hazard and an indecency.
interject name:silas_vane: Roses by the bushel and a chandelier like a high roller's table. This whole room's a rig.
interject name:rook_coldwake: A journal left open, and a painting of an elven woman right beside the channel. No proper clerk does that.
interject name:silas_vane: He painted her like a winning hand he lost on the turn of one card.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the edge, Silas. Polished stone goes slick when the air's this damp.
endif
-> END

~ mon_cathedral_moon_06_cordelia_lucan
if name:cordelia_skein and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mon_cathedral_moon and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: The blood moon pours through the red and violet glass like a stained slide. Lovely.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The scent of old iron is pressing hard behind my eyes, Cordelia. Keep your voice low, if you please.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your pulse is past a hundred, though your diction stays crisp. Shall I stand between you and the statue?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Thank you, yes. I'd hate a snarl to spoil my grading of the altar. Barnaby's behind my boots.
endif
-> END

~ mon_ground_07_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and at:mon_ground and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The roses haven't wilted an inch, Rook, but the whole place feels like a hall after the curtain drops.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The racket's gone out of the stone. My door-knocker hasn't twitched since we came back.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Even the gate veteran looks like an usher waiting to sweep up programmes. I almost miss the tension.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Quiet is good for the mortar. Remind me to draw a breath before the gate.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Take two, Rook. I'll pluck a dry rose off the pulpit for my lining.
endif
-> END
